I suggest you consult the Supreme Court decision in _Wooley v.
Maynard_, in which a criminal defendant succeeded in overturning his
conviction for covering up the "Live Free or Die" motto on his NH
license plate.  The majority found that the criminal sanction amounted
to improper coercion violative of the correlative first amendment
right *not* to engage in speech.

